From a5155d9ddbb18430bcd8449b9cdde0a92d87da9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GPTware AI Team <dcmaxhome@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:45:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] Generator: batched speculative accept
 (EXL3_SD_BATCH_ACCEPT, default off)

Multi-user verify rounds accepted job by job: each job's window samplers launched and read back on their own, then
two rewind launch sets per job (conv copy-back, scan replay) with ~10 us of Python per layer and job. With
EXL3_SD_BATCH_ACCEPT=1 every batchable job's window samplers launch before any is accepted and one synchronize covers
the round; the target-side GDN rewinds of the round are deferred and settled together (GDNState.rewind_many ->
batched_rewind_flat: descriptor arrays built with numpy, the same two kernels). Per-job RNG draws, acceptance order and
the settled states are those of the serial loop.

Also: CustomSampler set reqs_past_ids from every step before alt() dropped the identity ones; TabbyAPI adds
repetition 1.0 / presence 0 / frequency 0 steps to every stack, so every sampler claimed to read past ids and the
batched readback port (EXL3_SD_BATCH_READBACK) never engaged. Under EXL3_SD_BATCH_ACCEPT the flag comes from the
steps that survive simplification.
